# What cron runs for the system, each line naming the user it runs as
# (crontab(5)): upstream's, whose /usr/adm/daily, weekly and monthly
# are this system's (usr/adm in the tree);
# and sendmail, which tries again each hour to deliver what is in its
# queue (/usr/spool/mqueue), as upstream has the daemon do, since the
# daemon is not run unless /etc/rc.conf says to.  The times are local,
# as /etc/localtime has it (zic(8)), or universal without it.
0,15,30,45 * * * *	root /usr/libexec/atrun
5 0 * * *	root	/bin/sh /usr/adm/daily 2>&1 | mail root
15 0 * * 7	root	/bin/sh /usr/adm/weekly 2>&1 | mail root
35 0 1 * *	root	/bin/sh /usr/adm/monthly 2>&1 | mail root
40 * * * *	root /usr/sbin/sendmail -q
